        "problem": "Calculate $\\frac{2}{3}M+2N$, where\n$M=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 15 \\\\ -12 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$N=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & \\frac{1}{2} & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n| $\\frac{2}{3}M+2N=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $-2$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-12$ | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |",
        "worked_solution": "We multiply each entry of $M$ by $\\frac{2}{3}$ and each entry of $N$ by $2,$ and then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}M+2N & =\\frac{2}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 15 \\\\ -12 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & \\frac{1}{2} & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 6 & \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 0 & \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 15 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-12) & \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 6 & \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot 3 & 2\\cdot (-1) & 2\\cdot 0 \\\\ 2\\cdot (-2) & 2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} & 2\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4+6 & 0-2 & 10+0 \\\\ -8-4 & 4+1 & 0-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & -2 & 10 \\\\ -12 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
